WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.468
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.260
FERNANDO GARCIA: You
do want to be inspired

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.810
from the very beginning.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.960
Creative collaboration was
happening since the day we met.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.140
LAURA KIM: The way Fernando
starts his process by sketching

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.920
and the way I start my process
by draping or cutting fabric,

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.090
but we're ultimately ending
up at the same place.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.010
 I would definitely
recommend latching

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.220
onto people that are
strong enough to push you,

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.900
but also vulnerable enough
to listen to your ideas.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.160
 What I learned about how
to be a leader from Oscar

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.840
was he was always having fun.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.310
We were always laughing.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:42.060
I think that's very important
in a creative environment.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.650
This class is not just
for fashion students,

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.340
but also for people who
want to start a business

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.112
with a partner in any industry.

00:00:49.112 --> 00:00:50.820
 In this class, we're
going to teach you

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.080
how Laura and I work together.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.370
LAURA KIM: We're
going to do fittings.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.480
FERNANDO GARCIA: How
we design a collection.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.698
LAURA KIM: How you sketch.

00:00:55.698 --> 00:00:57.240
FERNANDO GARCIA:
How we build a team.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.380
LAURA KIM: How I drape.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.610
FERNANDO GARCIA: I think
no matter what, you just

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.530
need to be comfortable
to be around somebody

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:02.640
who can challenge you.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.170
 I think those
honest conversations

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.117
makes us good partners.

00:01:06.117 --> 00:01:07.700
FERNANDO GARCIA:
When we both started,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.580
we didn't understand what it
was like to launch a brand.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:14.480
And we realized that designing
was perhaps 50% of the time.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:18.200
 I get inspired a lot by
just random people walking by.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.420
Could be like a picture
of a really cute dog.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:24.920
 Or a hot guy on
a beach that I saw.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.290
 If you were to start
your own business,

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:30.290
you should really understand
who you are as a person

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:34.340
and find someone who can
do stuff that you can't do.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:37.460
FERNANDO GARCIA: That
might be the next runway.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:38.840
 I'm Laura Kim.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.100
 I'm Fernando Garcia.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.060
 And this is MasterClass.

